{
  "protocol": 1,
  "batch_id": "internode-logical-ag03-001",
  "mode": "dist",
  "supersedes": null,
  "requires": {
    "sm": 90,
    "gpus": 2,
    "env": "triton-dist"
  },
  "timeout_s": 900,
  "notes": [
    "Tutorial 03 of Triton-distributed 7908e4ea (inter-node all-gather): its kernels all_gather_push_1d_kernel and all_gather_push_2d_kernel, unchanged, on 64 bytes, 2 ranks. one_node/* is the control under triton-dist; logical_nodes/* runs 2 logical nodes of 1 rank.",
    "Expected, judged on the development side only (experiments/interp_gpu/internode_logical/judge.py): every test ok; every rank returns the 64 input bytes.",
    "The harness runs the tutorial functions, not the tutorial program: the file has no __main__ guard. It gives each signal tensor one word per rank; the tutorial program allocates one word and its kernels address word WORLD_SIZE - 1. See harness.py and documents/GpuInterNodeRuns.md.",
    "Meant for an NVLink pair, as internode-logical-env-002 ran on."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "id": "one_node/push_1d",
      "frontend": "triton-dist",
      "entry": "experiments/interp_gpu/internode_logical/harness.py::all_gather",
      "launch": {
        "kernel": "push_1d"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "x",
          "dtype": "int8",
          "shape": [
            64
          ],
          "gen": {
            "class": "normal",
            "seed": 1
          },
          "sha256": "e7dbc37ca408aa79d667169e9a2bbf875e980a01428c6216fbd7ab4a17b5019f"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "topology",
          "dtype": "int32",
          "shape": [
            6
          ],
          "sentinel": "0x80000000"
        },
        {
          "name": "gathered",
          "dtype": "int8",
          "shape": [
            64
          ],
          "sentinel": "0x80"
        }
      ],
      "reference": {
        "kind": "none"
      },
      "ranks": 2,
      "launcher": "triton-dist",
      "repeats": 2
    },
